      "id": "page-components-spacer",
      "slug": "components/spacer",
      "slug_locked": false,
      "head": {
        "title": "Spacer component Breakdown",
        "meta_title": "Spacer component Breakdown | ldnddev Framework",
        "meta_description": "The dd-spacer component provides a simple way to add vertical spacing or dividers between elements, helping control layout flow without custom CSS.",
        "canonical_url": null,
        "robots": "index, follow",
        "schema_type": "WebPage",
        "og_title": null,
        "og_description": null,
        "og_image": null
      },
      "nodes": [
        {
          "node_type": "section",
          "id": "page-components-spacer-section-1",
          "section_title": null,
          "section_class": "-full-lg",
          "item_box_class": "l-box",
          "sal": "no-animation",
          "columns": [
            {
              "id": "page-components-spacer-section-1-column-1",
              "width_class": "dd-u-1-1",
              "components": [
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "# Spacer component Breakdown"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "## Overview\n\nThe dd-spacer component provides a simple way to add vertical spacing or dividers between elements, helping control layout flow without custom CSS. It supports predefined sizes and an optional divider line, making it a utility for consistent padding in sections, grids, or between components.\n\nThis component is ideal for adding breathing room in content-heavy areas or separating blocks visually. In WordPress, configure it via an ACF select field for size and divider options within flexible content. In Drupal, use a Paragraph type with a select field for size and a boolean for divider, rendering as a standalone element.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nUse a div with class *dd-spacer* and a size modifier like *-xl*. Add *-divider* for a horizontal line.\n\n```\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xl -divider\"></div>\n```\n\nPlace it between elements or sections for spacing; it's full-width by default and can be nested in grids or sections."
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "### Preview"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "<div class=\"dd-example\">\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -sm\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -md -divider\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -lg\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xl\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xxl\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xxxl\"></div>\n</div>"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "### Code"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "```html\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -sm\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -md -divider\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -lg\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xl\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xxl\"></div>\n<div class=\"dd-spacer -xxxl\"></div>\n```"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "## CSS Modifiers (from _dd_spacer.scss)\n\nThe SCSS file defines base styles for the spacer as a block element with relative positioning and 100% width. Key modifiers include:\n\n- *-sm*: Adds 0.5rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-md*: Adds 1rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-lg*: Adds 1.5rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-xl*: Adds 2rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-xxl*: Adds 2.5rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-xxxl*: Adds 3rem top/bottom margin.\n- *-divider*: Adds a 1px solid border (colored via primary variable).\n\nFor ACF/Paragraphs integration, use select fields to apply size and divider classes dynamically.\n\n## Framework files\n\n- source/scss/components/_dd_spacer.scss (styles)\n\n## Accessibility and Best Practices\n\nAvoid overusing spacers; prefer semantic spacing via CSS margins/padding. For dividers, ensure they don't create empty landmarks. Use aria-hidden if decorative. Test for consistent flow in screen readers. In CMS, limit options to predefined sizes for design consistency and prevent abuse."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "page-components-tabs",
      "slug": "components/tabs",
      "slug_locked": false,
      "head": {
        "title": "Tabs Component Breakdown",
        "meta_title": "Tabs Component Breakdown | ldnddev Framework",
        "meta_description": "The dd-tabs component provides a tabbed interface for organizing content into switchable panels.",
        "canonical_url": null,
        "robots": "index, follow",
        "schema_type": "WebPage",
        "og_title": null,
        "og_description": null,
        "og_image": null
      },
      "nodes": [
        {
          "node_type": "section",
          "id": "page-components-tabs-section-1",
          "section_title": null,
          "section_class": "-full-lg",
          "item_box_class": "l-box",
          "sal": "no-animation",
          "columns": [
            {
              "id": "page-components-tabs-section-1-column-1",
              "width_class": "dd-u-1-1",
              "components": [
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "# Tabs Component Breakdown"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "## Overview\n\nThe *dd-tabs* component provides a tabbed interface for\norganizing content into switchable panels. It supports desktop\nnavigation and a mobile dropdown menu, with ARIA attributes for\naccessibility, making it suitable for FAQs, product details, or\nmulti-section content without page reloads.\n\nThis component is ideal for content-heavy pages where space-saving is\nkey. In WordPress, configure it via ACF repeater fields for tab items\n(e.g., label, content, links). In Drupal, use a Paragraph type with\nfields for tab titles and bodies, rendered with unique data-id for\nscoping multiple instances.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nWrap tabs in a div with class *dd-tabs* and a unique data-id.\nInclude navigation with menu items (ARIA roles) and content panels\nwith aria-hidden and role=\"tabpanel\"."
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "### Preview"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "<div class=\"dd-example\">\n<div class=\"dd-tabs\" data-id=\"003\">\n  <div class=\"dd-tabs__content dd-g\">\n    <ul class=\"dd-tabs__menu dd-g\" role=\"tablist\">\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a  class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link -active\" id=\"tab-001\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-001\">open tab 1</a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a href=\"#tab-002\" class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link\" id=\"tab-002\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-002\">open tab 2</a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a href=\"#tab-003\" class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link\" id=\"tab-003\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-003\">open tab 3</a>\n      </li>\n    </ul>\n    <div class=\"dd-tabs__items dd-g\">\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1 -active\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-001\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-001\">\n        <p>tab panel 001</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-002\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-002\">\n        <p>tab panel 002</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-003\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-003\">\n        <p>tab panel 003</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "### Code"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "```html\n<div class=\"dd-tabs\" data-id=\"003\">\n  <div class=\"dd-tabs__content dd-g\">\n    <ul class=\"dd-tabs__menu dd-g\" role=\"tablist\">\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a  class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link -active\" id=\"tab-001\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-001\">open tab 1</a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a href=\"#tab-002\" class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link\" id=\"tab-002\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-002\">open tab 2</a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"dd-tabs__menu-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n        <a href=\"#tab-003\" class=\"dd-tabs__menu-link\" id=\"tab-003\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"tabpanel-003\">open tab 3</a>\n      </li>\n    </ul>\n    <div class=\"dd-tabs__items dd-g\">\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1 -active\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-001\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-001\">\n        <p>tab panel 001</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-002\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-002\">\n        <p>tab panel 002</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"dd-tabs__item dd-u-1-1\" role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"tabpanel-003\" aria-hidden=\"false\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-003\">\n        <p>tab panel 003</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```"
                },
                {
                  "component_type": "rich_text",
                  "parent_class": null,
                  "sal": "no-animation",
                  "parent_copy": "Use unique IDs for tabs and panels; JS handles switching and\nmobile toggle.\n\n## CSS Modifiers (from _dd_tabs.scss)\n\nThe SCSS file defines base styles for tabs, including\nresponsive navigation (hidden menu on mobile), active states,\nand overflow handling. Key modifiers include:\n\n- *-active*: Applied to active menu items and panels\n  for visibility and styling.\n- *-horizontal*: Adjusts for horizontal tab layouts if\n  extended.\n- *-vertical*: For vertical tab orientations (sidebar\n  style).\n- Utility classes like SAL data attributes (e.g.,\n  *data-sal=\"fade\"*) for panel animations.\n\n## Associated JavaScript (from dd_tabs.js)\n\nThe component includes a JS file handling mobile menu toggle\nand tab switching with ARIA updates. Key features:\n\n- Toggles -active class on mobile menu open/close.\n- Switches tabs on click, updating aria-selected, aria-hidden,\n  and active classes, scoped by aria-controls.\n- Updates mobile placeholder text to current tab label.\n- Supports multiple tab groups on a page via aria-controls and\n  panel ID.\n\nInclude the JS via your CMS: In WordPress, enqueue in\nfunctions.php; in Drupal, attach via libraries.yml.\n\nFor ACF/Paragraphs integration, generate unique aria-controls\nfrom fields.\n\n## Framework files\n\n- source/js/components/_dd_tabs.js (javascript)\n- source/scss/components/_dd_tabs.scss (styles)\n\n## Accessibility and Best Practices\n\nUse ARIA roles (tablist, tab, tabpanel) and attributes\n(aria-selected, aria-controls, aria-labelledby, aria-hidden).\nEnsure keyboard navigation (focus on tabs, enter/space to\nactivate). Test with screen readers for announcements. In CMS,\nrequire unique labels and validate content for empty panels."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
